          <annot type="general_description">
            <p>(a) TumW C.5.1 to TumW C.5.27, TumW D.3.2, and TumW D.2.1 are transmitted in a single collection in A-Wgm. In addition, TumW C.5.1 to TumW C.5.15 are also collected in a later copy in D-Dl. Thus, these two sources are only fully described in the metadata for TumW C.5.1.</p>
            <p>(b) Most of the responsories TumW C.5.1 to 27 follow the classical ternary structure, i.e., chorus (consisting of two parts)&#x2013;solo verse&#x2013;repetendum (the second part of the respond repeated), or ABCB. Some responsories have an extended structure ABCBAB. In the description of the music, the total number of bars always refers to the sum of bars in ABC.</p>
          </annot>
