        <itemList>
          <item>
            <identifier/>
            <physDesc>
              <extent>70 fol.</extent>
              <titlePage label="[fol. 1r = p. 1]">
                <p>H&#xE6;c | Responsoria | Cum Psalmis Miserere, et Benedictus | Pro Matutinis Hebdomad&#xE6; Sacr&#xE6; Con&#xE6; Domini, Parasceves | et Sabbathi Sancti &#xE2; Pr&#xE6;nobili Domino Francisco Tuma | Augusti&#x17F;sim&#xE6; Imperatricis Elisabeth&#xE6; Chori Musici Pr&#xE6;- | fecto in Contrapunctis cum Clavi-Cymbalo composita | prima vice producta sunt in Sacra Hebdomada | 1759.</p>
              </titlePage>
              <titlePage label="[p. 3]">
                <p>R.1.</p>
              </titlePage>
              <dimensions>
                <locusGrp>
                  <locus/>
                </locusGrp>
                <height quantity="22" unit="cm">22 (height in cm)</height>
                <width quantity="31" unit="cm">31 (height in cm)</width>
                <term/>
                <extent> lines</extent>
              </dimensions>
              <dimensions/>
              <handList>
                <hand xmlns:xl="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink" xmlns:xs="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema" medium="brown ink" type="main">unidentified</hand>
              </handList>
              <physMedium>
                <p>Source consists of a full score bound in brown marbled cardboard and comprises 70 leaves. Each recto page is numbered in the upper right corner. Contents: p. 1: title; p. 2: empty; p. 3&#x2013;36: music (TumW C.5.1 to TumW C.5.9; caption title on p. 3: &#x201C;Responsoria pro Hebdomada Sancta in Coena Domini.&#x201D;; hand-ruled paper, 12 staves (7 mm) in light brown ink and music in same ink); p. 37&#x2013;38: empty; p. 39&#x2013;79: music (TumW C.5.10 to TumW C.5.18; caption title on p. 39: &#x201C;In Parasceve.&#x201D;); p. 80: empty; p. 81&#x2013;113: music (TumW C.5.19 to TumW C.5.29; caption title on p. 81: &#x201C;Pro Sabbatho Sancto.&#x201D;); p. 114: empty; p. 115&#x2013;129: music (TumW D.3.1; caption title on p. 115: &#x201C;Miserere.&#x201D;); p. 130: empty; p. 131&#x2013;137: music (TumW D.2.1; no title); p. 138: empty; and p. 139&#x2013;140: composer's note.</p>
                <p>The composer's note is: [fol. 70r = p. 139] Notanda Compositoris. | In primis omnis versus hoc signo notatus V. a vocibus Solis et non reduplica- | tis cantari debet, et in mensura temporis tardiori, reliqua vero cantantur | in pleno, et sub mensura velociori. Requiruntur autem tres ad minimum Te- | norist&#xE6; et Ba&#x17F;sist&#xE6; ad productionem huius operis, ut bonum sortiatur effec- | tum. Deinde Cantaros et pr&#xE6;cipue pueri per laborem indefe&#x17F;sum debent | instrui ut rem cum summa facilitate sciant decantare, et ideo frequen- | tes prob&#xE6; instituend&#xE6;, et labori tamdiu insistendum, donec res ad votum | succedat: alias enim compositio audientibus fieret insipida, et labor | meus irritus. In locis ubi signatum est Adagio et piano debet vox in | tractu suo jam augeri jam diminui, sed tamen cum comuni omnium | Cantorum annutu, et intelligentia, et eodem momento ab omnibus | exequatur. Hoc pr&#xE6;cipue potest effici in notis longioris valoris, [fol. 70v = p. 140] quia sunt majoris durationis, et extensionis. Un&#xF4; verb&#xF4; | ejusmodi compositiones sunt difficillim&#xE6; productionis, et | ideo maximam exercitationem requirunt.</p>
              </physMedium>
            </physDesc>
